From: VIMS Coder <346484346+VIMS-Coder@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] reqwest: trust the system certificate store too

reqwest's `rustls-tls` feature trusts only the roots compiled into the
binary, ignoring SSL_CERT_FILE and the system store. Behind a TLS-
inspecting egress proxy (VIMS' sandbox envelope, a corporate proxy) every
HTTPS request then fails with "unknown certificate authority".
`rustls-tls-native-roots` adds the platform store (rustls-native-certs,
which honours SSL_CERT_FILE / SSL_CERT_DIR) next to the bundled roots.

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 554d9a3..0a2908a 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ clap = { version = "4", features = ["derive"] }
 clap_complete = "4"
 
 # HTTP client (for LLM drivers)
-reqwest = { version = "0.12", default-features = false, features = ["json", "stream", "multipart", "rustls-tls", "gzip", "deflate", "brotli"] }
+reqwest = { version = "0.12", default-features = false, features = ["json", "stream", "multipart", "rustls-tls", "rustls-tls-native-roots", "gzip", "deflate", "brotli"] }
 rustls = { version = "0.23", default-features = false, features = ["ring"] }
 
 # Async trait
